[0m$ [0mcd "/home/nico/Documents/U/Co/U/4s/courses/interfaces/tareas/proyecto final/juego" && git add -A && git commit -q -m "Gameplay, rendering, AI and three levels; headless smoke check passes

Coordinates: +y is up everywhere. The physics originally treated +y as down
while the ortho camera treated it as up, which rendered the whole level
upside down with the player standing on the ceiling. Jump reach is now derived
explicitly in config.js and the level geometry is built inside it.

Rendering: the post pass encodes linear -> sRGB. Sprite textures are tagged
sRGB so the scene pass samples into linear, and a raw ShaderMaterial writing
to the default framebuffer gets no automatic encode -- the game was rendering
about a stop and a half dark until that was added.

Sprites: quantise to a fixed 8-colour per-level palette, which turned Kael's
brown and blue into emerald and made the hero vanish into the shrine. Replaced
with a colour-depth posterise plus a per-level grade.

Geometry: sprite quads are shifted into 0..1 before the cell scale is applied.
Translating by baseline/2 stretched each quad to ~48x its cell and parked the
sprites off-screen.

ai.js: decide() referenced `player` without receiving it.

assets/bg/ is opt-in via a manifest rather than probing for files, so an empty
folder does not log a 404 on every load." && git log --oneline | head -3
